r from the docs is a low follow-up outside AC11's stated content.","id":"R11","outcome":"PASS"}],"dimensions":[{"evidence":"I re-read follow-ups.js in full (derivation, the gate-aware unavailable logic, redactor/publicRedaction/redactedRecords, decide, render, followUpLines), publication.js reviewTarget and withFollowUps, workflow-projection.js followUpRows and projectWorkflow, and the convergence.js measure-2 filter. The redactor path regex leaves repository-relative paths such as app/app.js intact (the lookbehind rejects a word character before the slash), and record.repository and IDs are not redacted. Withdrawal is idempotent (outcome WITHDRAWN check) and a follow-up that qualifies again restores followUp with outcome undefined. The only replay edge I found is a stale followUp on a merged in-pass row after a projection-version upgrade; that needs an imported pre-v3 row carrying followUp, so it is not realistic and is not raised. No supported defect at medium or high.","name":"code","outcome":"PASS"},{"evidence":"R1-R11 all pass on current tests and source (see criteria). Both round-1 rubric gaps (R1 present-after-fixed, R7 written by decide) are now tested. Amendment 1 (latest report, own-name exception, follow-up rows) is unchanged and still tested. Project rule from the spec Definition of Done: the CLI suite passes (receipt 1: 724 tests, 723 pass, 1 skipped, 0 fail, with the documented host-dependent exclusions) and the desktop mirrors match (copies-match test passed). The scratchpad decisions S4-S6 are consistent with the implementation.","name":"requirements","outcome":"PASS"},{"evidence":"All five receipts ran on 8408c338 (the candidate head): focused follow-up and convergence tests, 33/33 pass (receipt 0, including the new withdrawal, present-reopen and decide-render tests); CLI suite 724/723 pass, 1 skipped (receipt 1); plugin validate and lint (receipts 2-3); desktop contract 185/185 (receipt 4). Every changed source area in this round (follow-ups.js, pu